WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:19.750
While the secret garden was coming alive and two children were coming alive with it, Mr.

2
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.452
Craven was wandering through Europe.

3
00:00:24.293 --> 00:00:26.895
He had traveled through the beautiful mountains of Switzerland.

4
00:00:28.596 --> 00:00:31.058
He had seen the magnificent Norwegian fjords.

5
00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:37.146
But his heart was still broken, and he could not shake the dark thoughts and nightmares from his

6
00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:42.609
mind. One day he was hiking in Austria when he decided to rest by a stream.

7
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.093
Mr. Craven did not know how long he sat there on the carpet of green moss, looking at

8
00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.293
the birds and the flowers.

9
00:00:50.554 --> 00:00:52.575
The sunlight seemed to wash over him.

10
00:00:52.595 --> 00:00:55.297
"What's happening?"

11
00:00:55.717 --> 00:00:56.258
he whispered.

12
00:00:56.278 --> 00:01:00.080
"I feel Why, it's almost as if I were awakening!"

13
00:01:01.296 --> 00:01:05.600
Months later he would find out that this was the very day when Colin stood in the garden

14
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.803
and said, "I'm going to live forever and ever!"

15
00:01:10.444 --> 00:01:12.706
As summer changed into autumn, Mr.

16
00:01:12.726 --> 00:01:15.288
Craven moved on to Lake Como in Italy.

17
00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:19.892
He was starting to sleep better, and his dreams no longer terrified him.

18
00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:24.376
He began to think of Misselthwaite and wonder if he should go home.

19
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:28.800
But every time he thought of Colin, he was reminded of his wife.

20
00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:31.137
He couldn't go home yet.

21
00:01:32.918 --> 00:01:34.739
One night he sat outside by the lake.

22
00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:37.820
The moonlight turned everything to silver.

23
00:01:38.941 --> 00:01:40.222
Mr. Craven fell asleep.

24
00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:43.624
In his dreams he heard a voice calling him.

25
00:01:44.864 --> 00:01:47.166
"Archie! Archie!"

26
00:01:48.406 --> 00:01:52.829
It was a sweet and lovely voice that he instantly recognized as his wife's.

27
00:01:52.849 --> 00:01:55.150
"Where are you?"

28
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.272
"In the garden."

29
00:01:59.584 --> 00:02:02.465
The dream ended there, but he did not wake up until morning.

30
00:02:03.725 --> 00:02:07.646
A servant appeared by his side and handed him a letter from Dickon's mother.

31
00:02:09.147 --> 00:02:12.067
Dear Sir: Please come home.

32
00:02:13.488 --> 00:02:15.308
I think you will be glad if you do.

33
00:02:16.529 --> 00:02:21.770
If you will excuse me, sir, I think your lady would ask you to come if she was

34
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:27.732
here. Sincerely, Susan Sowerby Mr.

35
00:02:27.772 --> 00:02:29.092
Craven remembered his dream.

36
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.642
"I must go home to Misselthwaite at once," he said to the servant.

37
00:02:37.705 --> 00:02:38.126
When Mr.

38
00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:41.648
Craven finally arrived at the manor, he immediately sent for Mrs.

39
00:02:41.688 --> 00:02:45.691
Medlock. "How is Colin?"

40
00:02:47.592 --> 00:02:49.714
Mrs. Medlock didn't know how to respond.

41
00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:57.860
"To tell the truth, sir," she said nervously, "he might be better and he might be worse.

42
00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.902
No one can understand why he eats or doesn't eat.

43
00:03:03.164 --> 00:03:04.765
He likes Mary and Dickon.

44
00:03:06.106 --> 00:03:11.150
Every day he goes outside with them, but no one knows what they do or where they go."

45
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.672
"Where is Colin now?"

46
00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:17.155
"In one of the gardens, I suppose."

47
00:03:17.175 --> 00:03:19.837
"In the garden," Mr.

48
00:03:19.877 --> 00:03:21.458
Craven repeated as he stood up.

49
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.563
He felt as if he were being pulled toward the garden that he had locked up ten years

50
00:03:27.623 --> 00:03:33.677
ago. He went outside and walked past the old fountain.

51
00:03:34.937 --> 00:03:38.018
Flowers surrounded it now, and it was filled with water.

52
00:03:39.258 --> 00:03:42.139
He turned down the long path outside the walled gardens.

53
00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:46.541
He knew where the door was, even though it was hidden by ivy.

54
00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.001
But could he find the key?

55
00:03:50.242 --> 00:03:51.362
He stopped and listened.

56
00:03:52.742 --> 00:03:57.684
No one had passed through that door in ten years, yet it sounded like children were laughing in

57
00:03:57.724 --> 00:03:58.144
the garden.

58
00:03:59.796 --> 00:04:00.896
Was this another dream?

59
00:04:02.197 --> 00:04:04.777
At that moment the door to the garden flew open.

60
00:04:06.018 --> 00:04:08.618
A boy ran out and crashed right into Mr.

61
00:04:08.638 --> 00:04:10.639
Craven. Mr.

62
00:04:10.679 --> 00:04:11.879
Craven stared at the boy.

63
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.561
His eyes were so dark, so like her eyes But it couldn't be.

64
00:04:17.581 --> 00:04:21.302
"Father, I'm Colin," said the boy.

65
00:04:21.322 --> 00:04:23.423
"I know you can't believe it.

66
00:04:24.443 --> 00:04:25.923
I can scarcely believe it myself."

67
00:04:25.943 --> 00:04:29.256
"In the garden," said Mr.

68
00:04:29.296 --> 00:04:31.698
Craven, unable to say anything else.

69
00:04:31.718 --> 00:04:35.300
"Yes. It was the garden that made me well.

70
00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:36.901
And Mary.

71
00:04:37.181 --> 00:04:38.642
And Dickon and his creatures.

72
00:04:38.962 --> 00:04:39.542
And magic."

73
00:04:40.783 --> 00:04:44.285
Colin was breathless from running, and his words came tumbling out.

74
00:04:45.666 --> 00:04:46.426
"I'm really well.

75
00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.207
I just beat Mary in a race.

76
00:04:49.408 --> 00:04:51.409
Father, I'm going to live forever and ever.

77
00:04:51.809 --> 00:04:52.550
Aren't you glad?"

78
00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.372
Mr. Craven did not know what to say for a moment.

79
00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.441
He put his hands on Colin's shoulders.

80
00:04:59.461 --> 00:05:02.342
"You must tell me all about it."

81
00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:06.244
And so Colin led him into the secret garden.

82
00:05:07.444 --> 00:05:13.526
Mr. Craven looked around, just as Colin had done his first time there, marveling at the roses and

83
00:05:13.626 --> 00:05:14.327
other flowers.

84
00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.948
"I thought it would all be dead."

85
00:05:18.929 --> 00:05:20.569
Mary and Dickon sat with Mr.

86
00:05:20.609 --> 00:05:24.411
Craven while Colin told the story of how they brought the garden back to life.

87
00:05:25.551 --> 00:05:29.205
Ben Weatherstaff was there too, but he soon slipped back to the house.

88
00:05:30.485 --> 00:05:33.126
He wanted to be in the servants' hall when Colin returned.

89
00:05:34.587 --> 00:05:36.448
After a while Ben went to the window.

90
00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:40.149
"Look what's coming across the grass."

91
00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.310
When Mrs.

92
00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.671
Medlock looked, she let out a little shriek.

93
00:05:47.232 --> 00:05:49.213
All the other servants ran to the window.

94
00:05:51.134 --> 00:05:52.534
Across the lawn came Mr.

95
00:05:52.594 --> 00:05:54.655
Craven, laughing and smiling.

96
00:05:55.795 --> 00:06:00.303
And walking by his side, as tall and straight as any boy, was
